Well, you're entitled to your opinion, and I can certainly sympathize with
you. I do enjoy have an elite group of friends with whom I can party and
enjoy listening to. (I've certainly never encountered a group of people
that was so good at making feel stupid and challenging me to grow, how
delightful!) Growth could potentially challenge that, making parties large
enough to become unmanageable, etc. On the other hand, I think core groups
will appear and start having smaller parties with just their ExI-friends
over, in fact I think this already starting to happen.

I can, however, see some major advantages to more extropians. It's hard to
effect social change as such a small minority for one thing. For another,
it would be great to have small, bay-area-like enclaves of extropians to
travel to and from. Mondo extropaganza hoping as a permanent tourist any
one? Don't forget Extropia, either. (Yes, I know, in cypherspace first, but
I want one in RL some time after.)

I hope you don't mind too terribly if the Extropians expand, because its
happening, and many of us are behind it.

