Robin Hanson uses an analogy:

 * Genome + development == assembly language and hardware
 * Computer programs == C code

Where the phenotype is "intelligence" and the "task" is porting from
assembly to C.

> I say I`m going to play with this assembly language, writing things in
> it and executing them, until I figure out the language, and then write a
> translater from this language to C.  I claim I can get to a work-alike
> faster than you, though I admit mine is likely to run slower.  You
> counter by pointing out that I have never even ported a 100 line
> program from this assembly language to C.  
> 
