on what we dream might be, losing our grip on improving our lot in the 
world as it is: the social democratic world we are all wrapped up in --
paying taxes, using the roads, depending on police protection,
college financial aid, some of us even work for the government, 
ad nauseum.  Tim May has called us "elite", but most of us much more
skilled in dreaming about the world as it might be than in 
working with the world as it is.  Detweiling the poor, dreaming of 
PPLs and the next century's tech gadgets(1), etc. can be quite 
entertaining and interesting, but are mostly useless for building for 
our future in the world as we find it today.

